  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "Final rules keep S1 deadlines tight (24h serious, 7 days other, 3 days customer notice) but limit non-serious reporting to confirmed incidents. S2 retains 55°C/5% but allows continued sales with regulator discretion and no public per-model rates, while customers get numeric rates. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit pathway; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notices."
